{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1083","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. The Fair Nut and Rectangles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Fair Nut got stacked in planar world. He should solve this task to get out."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given $$$n$$$ rectangles with vertexes in $$$(0, 0)$$$, $$$(x_i, 0)$$$, $$$(x_i, y_i)$$$, $$$(0, y_i)$$$. For each rectangle, you are also given a number $$$a_i$$$. Choose some of them that the area of union minus sum of $$$a_i$$$ of the chosen ones is maximum."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that there are no nested rectangles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nut has no idea how to find the answer, so he asked for your help."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 10^6$$$) — the number of rectangles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$n$$$ lines contains three integers $$$x_i$$$, $$$y_i$$$ and $$$a_i$$$ ($$$1 \\leq x_i, y_i \\leq 10^9$$$, $$$0 \\leq a_i \\leq x_i \\cdot y_i$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that there are no nested rectangles."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single line print the answer to the problem — the maximum value which you can achieve."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n4 4 8\n1 5 0\n5 2 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n9"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n6 2 4\n1 6 2\n2 4 3\n5 3 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the right answer can be achieved by choosing the first and the second rectangles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, the right answer can also be achieved by choosing the first and the second rectangles."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1083E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1083/problem/E"}